\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  Not human advice nor wisdom's command
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj Can help you to reach the Heavenly land
\par In dust must the pilgrim, discouraged,  abide
\par If fail the assurance:
\par  The Lord will provide, the Lord will provide.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. When, longing, your eyes look up to the light,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Confessing to God your heart is not right,
\par  Then shall His compassion upon you abide
\par Be joyful, O pilgrim,
\par  The Lord will provide, the Lord will provide.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Thy heart He has known forever and e'er;
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj He weighs all thy pain and justly does  share;
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 What's good for His children the Lord shall decide.
\par As saviour, from downfall,
\par The Lord will provide, the Lord will provide.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. 'Tis easy to walk, whatever your stand
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj For Jesus will kindly lend you His hand.
\par Thro' night and day dawning, o'er hills and the tide
\par  Shines brightly the promise:
\par The Lord will provide, the Lord will  provide.\tab\i 
\par \pard\i0\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

